{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789820988,"nonce":"fqIpcVY1Xj5AAuwjD6UJStj4m+w=","title":"Python array module: what the typed arrays still leave out","message":"Landed: `array.array` as `List(Elem::Array(Code))` with exact-width\nstorage per typecode, CPython's OverflowError wording, f32 rounding,\nrepr with the typecode, tolist/fromlist/extend/append/insert/pop/remove/\nindex/count/reverse, typecode and itemsize, slicing, repeat, concat,\ncomparisons, membership, sum/min/max/sorted/list/tuple, boxing under an\narray tag with dynamic repr/len/getitem/setitem/iter/eq/type.\n\nNot yet:\n- `Elem::Array` as a list element kind. A list of arrays (scimark's\n  ArrayList, `[array('d', [0]) * w for y in range(h)]`) is `List(Object)`\n  with boxed arrays; LU's `A[k][j]` goes through `zb_any_getitem_i64` and\n  a tag check per access. The fix is the nested element kind, the same\n  lever meteor's `fps` needs.\n- tobytes/frombytes/tofile/fromfile/buffer_info/byteswap: no bytes type\n  yet; raytrace-simple and crypto_pyaes need tobytes and array('B', bytes).\n- a float searched for in an integer array (`1.0 in array('i', [1])`) is\n  refused at compile time rather than compared numerically.\n- 'L'/'Q' elements at or above 2^63 print negative (int is i64);\n  'Q' reports a negative value with 'L's message.\n- a typecode held in a variable bound to one literal is refused; only a\n  literal typecode is accepted. Constant propagation through locals would\n  admit `code = 'd'; array(code, ...)`.\n- the conformance case pins CPython 3.14's `array.typecodes`\n  (`bBuwhHiIlLqQfd`); 3.9 prints it without `w`.","files":null}]}